children.body:
Reusable world volumes or authored artefacts that alter a controlled set of game rules.

Candidate channels:
- gravity direction / strength;
- object weight or force;
- movement / animation / simulation rate;
- biological growth or state;
- visibility / perception;
- sound filtering / pitch / time;
- fog, light, colour and post processing;
- object / collision state;
- water or environmental motion.

An effect should be authorable as a combination of channels rather than one bespoke code path per puzzle. This gives the design team a versatile 'strangeness vocabulary' while keeping rules consistent.
